{"name":"Nocturnal","hex":"#767d86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nocturnal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person, creature, group, or species, primarily active during the night.","Of an occurrence, taking place at night, nightly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or creature that is active at night.","A device for telling the time at night, rather like a sundial but read according to the stars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nocturnal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nocturnal (Heltah Skeltah album)","blocks":[{"text":"Nocturnal is the debut studio album by American hip hop duo Heltah Skeltah. It was released on June 18, 1996, via Duck Down/Priority Records. The recording sessions took place at Chung King Studios, at Dollar Cab, at D&D Studios, and at Unique Recording Studios in New York City. It was produced by Da Beatminerz, Buckshot, Shaleek, Shawn J. Period, Supreme, E-Swift, Lord Jamar and Sean Price. It features guest appearances from Originoo Gunn Clappaz, Illa Noyz, Representativz and Vinia Mojica. The album peaked at number 35 on the Billboard 200 and number 5 on the Top R&B/Hip-Hop Albums."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Nocturnal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nocturnal_(Heltah_Skeltah_album)","wikidata":"Q14867722"},{"title":"Nocturnal animal","blocks":[{"text":"Nocturnality is a behavior in some non-human animals characterized by being active during the night and sleeping during the day. The common adjective is nocturnal, with diurnal meaning the opposite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Owl_at_Night.jpg/330px-Owl_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nocturnal_animal","wikidata":"Q309179"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com